{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"xpath\" initial=\"a\">\n  <final id=\"a\">\n    <onentry>\n      <log expr=\"((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((1))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))\"/>\n    </onentry>\n  </final>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml040-xpath-over-nesting-bound.scxml"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml040-xpath-over-nesting-bound.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":419,"endLine":4,"startColumn":18,"startLine":4}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`expr` was declined by the data-model syntax checker\n\n**Note:** the data model applies the same bound when it evaluates this fragment, so it would be rejected at run time\n\n**Help:** split the expression into smaller ones, assigning intermediate results to `<data>` variables with `<assign>`, so each fragment stays within the bound\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions","text":"`expr` was declined by the data-model syntax checker"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":541,"start":140},"category":"semantic"},"ruleId":"SCXML040"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"the data-model syntax capability declines fragments beyond its size or nesting bound (the ECMAScript provider: 16 KiB expressions, 64 KiB scripts, at most 128 structural nesting units, where each open bracket costs 8, so 16 brackets, 15 inside a value expression) instead of risking its parser stack; the data model applies the same bound when it evaluates the fragment, so the fragment would be rejected at run time and `compile` refuses the document. The size bounds apply to wasm builds only (the shipped validator and data-model components; the native `scxml-cli` checks fragments of any size); the nesting bound guards the parser's native stack and applies to every build"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: split the expression or script into smaller parts, assigning intermediate results to variables (`<data>` or `<assign>`).\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML040` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#expressions","id":"SCXML040","name":"SCXML040","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an expression exceeds the data model's size or nesting bound"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}